d":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"type":"text","text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s (34 n from 5,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solver."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Traps when the work limit is spent: 4,000 + 20√n products on σI − L (then shift-invert),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1,000 shift-invert products, 20,000 + 2n per solve. Only a tolerance below rounding has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached it in the measurements."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"0 is no edge.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Precondition","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"At least two vertices, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Every weight is finite and nonnegative.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/fiedlerVector(weight:normalized:tolerance:)-6hc98","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Fiedler vector: λ₂ and a unit eigenvector of it, with the canonical sign (see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"FiedlerVector","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); nil when the graph is not connected. NetworkX "},{"code":"fiedler_vector","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols":{"title":"GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"title":"Edges","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","text":"Collection","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edges-swift.associatedtype","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/FiedlerVector":{"title":"FiedlerVector","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Fiedler vector of a connected graph: a unit eigenvector of λ₂, the algebr